Security hardening of untrusted input handling: device-supplied file names (FTP/SFTP listings, HTTP ``Content-Disposition``, Telnet task tables) and tar archive members are now confined to the output directory; pillage copies only regular files (no symlinks or device nodes, new ``pillage.max_file_size`` option) and mounts images with ``nodev,nosuid,noexec``; TLS certificate verification is on by default (new ``tls_verify``/``tls_ca_bundle`` settings and per-device ``https.verify`` option); SSH host keys are checked with trust-on-first-use (new ``ssh_known_hosts`` setting, ``ssh.host_key_fingerprint`` pinning); and device passwords are redacted from all logs instead of being written at the default log level.
